 the original consonantism to this day, e.g. Swabian Wefz, Bavarian Weps, Wepsn, Webasn, Webes. The spread of -sp- was reinforced, if not triggered, by Latin vespa. Popular association with the verb wispeln from Old High German hwispalōn (“to whir, to whisper”) is also likely; compare Central Franconian Wespel (“wasp”). Both the High German and the Low German forms go back to Proto-West Germanic *waspijā, a variant of *wapsu.\nCognates include Dutch wesp, English wasp, French guêpe. These are often traced back to Proto-Germanic *wapsō, from Proto-Indo-European *wobʰseh₂ (“wasp”), pertaining to *webʰ- (“to weave”). There are some formal problems to this particular reconstruction, however, most importantly the fact that Proto-Germanic *wapsō is an anomalous form lacking the expected effect of Primärberührung.",{"g":"f","decl":"||||n|n|n|n"}]],"senses":[[20547,"wespe","noun","wasp (insect)",0,"f"]]},"wimmelten":{"entries":[["wimmelten",null,null,null]],"senses":[[395417,"wimmelten","verb","inflection of wimmeln:",0],[395418,"wimmelten","verb","first/third-person plural preterite",1],[395419,"wimmelten","verb","first/third-person plural subjunctive II",2]],"inflections":[["wimmelten","wimmeln","first-person,indicative,plural,preterite"]]},"wohinter":{"entries":[["wohinter",null,null,null]],"senses":[[56511,"wohinter","adv","behind what",0]],"inflections":[["wohinter","hinter","error-unrecognized-form"]]},"übelnimmst":{"entries":[["übelnimmst",null,null,null]],"senses":[[648132,"übelnimmst","verb","second-person singular dependent present of übelnehmen",0]],"inflections":[["übelnimmst","übelnehmen","indicative,present,second-person,singular,subordinate-clause"]]},"überhörst":{"entries":[["überhörst",null,null,null]],"senses":[[647697,"überhörst","verb","second-person singular present of überhören",0]],"inflections":[["überhörst","überhören","indicative,present,second-person,singular"]]},"allophons":{"inflections":[["allophons","allophon","genitive"]]},"austrankst":{"infl